  other statement of the convention (Relation docstring, docs/graph-schema,
  discovery prompt, the open-vocabulary instruction in this same file) is
  upper-case; a lower-case default would have split the same predicate into
  two strings across runs and made the documented example query return
  nothing.
- The default path no longer renders &quot;## Allowed Relationships&quot; +=
 &quot;MUST be
  one of&quot;: `_format_relation_patterns` and `_relationship_type_instruc=
tion`
  take `strict=3D`; a declared `Ontology.relations` (enforced by `_prune`)
  keeps Allowed/MUST, while `relation_types` renders &quot;## Preferred
  Relationships&quot; and &quot;prefer one of ...; if none fits, use a desc=
riptive
  UPPER_SNAKE_CASE label&quot;. This makes the prompt match the documented
  &quot;guidance, not a filter&quot; semantics instead of suppressing domai=
n
  predicates, and gives off-list labels the same casing rule.
- Endpoint instruction restored to the *verified* entity list the model
  returns rather than &quot;the entity list above&quot; (the pre-extracted =
input),
  so relationships are not anchored to entities step 1 removed and then
  dropped for a missing endpoint.
- `relation_types` is validated like `entity_types`: labels are stripped
  and a blank/whitespace label raises ValueError instead of rendering as a
  bare &quot;- &quot; bullet.
- Docs: `relation_types` added to the GraphExtraction signature in
  api-reference.mdx; a &quot;Relation Types&quot; resolution section in
  extraction.mdx; ontology-discovery.mdx notes DEFAULT_RELATION_TYPES and
  that, unlike DEFAULT_ENTITY_TYPES, it is not seeded into the ontology
  graph. CHANGELOG &quot;Changed&quot; entries for the default vocabulary a=
nd the
  no-early-stop prompt.
- Tests: new TestRelationVocabularyInStep2Prompt drives `extract()` with a
  capturing LLM and covers the `if ontology.relations:` fork end to end
  (default reaches the step-2 prompt as Preferred/prefer; ontology
  relations override instance relation_types as Allowed/MUST;
  relation_types=3D[] leaves the vocabulary open; endpoint wording points a=
t
  the verified list). Helper tests updated for upper-case labels and the
  strict/non-strict rendering; blank-label and stripping tests added.
- .gitignore: drop the duplicate `graphrag_sdk/.venv` line inherited from
  merging the sibling PRs (one copy remains; the symlink stays untracked).

Not changed: surfacing the relation vocabulary to the Cypher-generation
schema block (review body follow-up) is explicitly out of scope for this
PR. The #309 facade cutover test already stubs extraction on main
(dda742e), so no CI change was needed here.

