falkordb 1.8.0 adds an optional `hiredis` extra that installs the C reply
parser. Retrieval reads each chunk's embedding back to rerank, and parsing
those replies in pure Python was most of the client CPU per question (about
48 ms, 11 ms with hiredis). Raise the floor to 1.8.0 so the extra exists.

