<blockquote>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>How these are computed.</strong> Per dataset, ACC i=
s the unweighted mean of the four
task-category scores, matching the <a href=3D"https://graphrag-bench.github=
.io/" rel=3D"nofollow">GraphRAG-Bench</a>
leaderboard convention:</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><code>Dataset ACC =3D (Fact Retrieval + Complex Reasoning +=
 Contextual Summarize + Creative Generation) / 4</code>
<code>Overall =3D (Novel ACC + Medical ACC) / 2</code></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Overall is our own summary across the two datasets; the lea=
derboard ranks each
dataset separately. Novel has 20 documents and 2,010 questions, Medical 1 c=
orpus
and 2,062 questions. FalkorDB scored August 2026 with <code>gpt-4o-mini</co=
de> (Azure OpenAI)
at temperature 0.7 for both graph construction and generation, <code>text-e=
mbedding-3-large</code>
at 1024 dimensions, text-to-Cypher retrieval enabled, and the benchmark's o=
wn
<code>generation_eval.py</code> unmodified as the judge. Competitor numbers=
 are from the
published leaderboard, unchanged. See <a href=3D"https://docs.falkordb.com/=
graphrag/graphrag-accuracy-benchmark" rel=3D"nofollow">the GraphRAG accurac=
y benchmark page</a>
for the full FalkorDB vs vector RAG comparison, configuration, reproduction
instructions and limitations, and <a href=3D"https://docs.falkordb.com/grap=
hrag/benchmark" rel=3D"nofollow">the benchmark methodology page</a> for
per-category results and the full 15-system comparison.</p>
</blockquote>
<p dir=3D"auto">Vectors match similar chunks. The graph traverses relations=
hips. Every answer cites its source.</p>
